// ==========================================================================================================================================================================================================
// Interface of the library to control a Thermo Scientific Cytomat
//
// Copyright (C) by HAMILTON Bonaduz AG
// All rights reserved.
// ==========================================================================================================================================================================================================
//
//  Modification History
//
//  2022-04-11   Janis Magnin: library created
//  2022-09-14:  v 1.0  Janis Magnin
//      - first release
//  2022-10-11:  v 1.1  Janis Magnin
//      - changes in function 'SetEnvironment': Input parameter no longer get checked if they are in a pre set range. They are only checked if they are of type float
//      - changes in function 'TowerShakerStart/TowerShakerStop': Range for storage position gets determined by the current maximum storage capacity of the device
//      - changes in function 'Initialize': At the end of the initialize a _WaitForReady is executed to ensure the device is finished initializing
//      - bugfix in function 'GetInventory': The Logic to determine if the storage position contains a Labware id was changed by implementing Hamilton_DriverTools::TrimRight
//  2023-02-08: v 1.2 Janis Magnin
//      - added new function 'MoveTransferStation': Allowes to move the transfer station
//      - added new funciton '_CommandWasSuccessful': Checks after every _SendCommand call if the returned message is successful
//      - changes in function '_HandleErrorMessage': return the error message if the input message was of type 'be' or 'er'
//  2023-02-15: v 1.3 Janis Magnin
//      - changes in function 'UpdateInventory': UpdateStatus parameter now accepts Int and string. This allowes to update the inventory with Labware IDs
//      - changes in function 'GetLabwareIDs': Trailing white spaces of the labware IDs were trimmed. Old: '1234         ', new: '1234'
//      - changes in function 'GetInventory': Trailing white spaces of the labware IDs were trimmed. Old: '1234         ', new: '1234'
//  2023-07-19: v1.4 Janis Magnin
//      - changes in library: removed private functions to check the different bits (busy, erro, ...) since only the _CheckBusyBit was used and it was confusing in the trace files.
//      - changes in function '_WaitForReady': The call of function _CheckState now returns all status bits (previously only the busy bit was returned).
//      - changes in variable 'TIMEOUT_SHORT': Changed from 10 to 20 seconds. 10 seconds could lead to errors if waitForFinish is not enabled.
//      - changes in function 'TowerShakerStart' and '_GetDeviceConfig': Added check for simulation mode.
//      - addition in function '_WaitForReady': Improved error messages depending on the error type (timeout/response) error.
//      - bugfix in function '_WaitForReady': When an error is present, the error bit is now reset. Before this, the Cytomat had to be restarted to reset the error bit.
//  2023-10-25: v1.5 Janis Magnin
//      - changes in function 'Initialize': During initialize the current date and time is queried and set.
//      - bugfix in function '_CommandWasSuccessful': Some serial cards generate an error 'er02' when sending the first command to the Cytomat. For this reason the response of the first command is ignored.
//  2023-12-14: v1.6 Janis Magnin
//      - changes in function 'GetLabwareIDs': Only the labware IDs of a stacker are now returned. Previously, the inventory management characters were also returned.
//      - added new function 'GetFirstFreeStoragePosition': Can be used to get the first empty position within the Cytomat.
//  2024-02-29: v1.7 Janis Magnin
//      - added new function 'GetFreeStoragePositions': Returns the number of free storage positions and the corresponding stacker/level positions
//  2024-04-17: v1.8 Janis Magnin
//      - changes in all inventory related functions: Depending if an P3 Sensor or Barcode reader is installed, the inventory functions are supported/not supported.
//      - changes in function 'StorePlateByPosition': If the cytomat does not support inventory management, the plate is stored without checking if the stacker space is free.
//      - addition of new private functions '_GetPlateDetectionMethod' and '_DeviceSupportsInventoryManagement': These allow to determine if the cytomat supports inventory management.
//      - bugfix in function '_WaitForReady': Error reset command is now sent after the error trace. Before, this would lead to wrong error trace messages.
//  2024-05-02: v1.9 Janis Magnin
//      - changes in function '_WaitForReady': In case of an error only false is returned. Before the library would automatically be terminated.
//      - changes in function '_HandlerErrorMessage': Changed return of the error message based on an request of the error register or if an error occured. Different errors are returned based on this.
//      - changes with constant 'CMD_OCCUPATION_STATUS': Changed command from ch:sc to ch:sd. The new command returns labware IDs with a max length of 32 characters instead of only 20 with ch:sc.
//      - changes in function 'Initialize': Cytomat type C24 is now also accepted.
//      - changes in functions 'GetPlateByLabwareID' 'GetPlateByPosition' and 'StorePlateByPosition'. It is now possible to store/get plates from a ToS without it having to shake.
//      - added new functions 'GetSpecificEnvironment' and 'SetSpecificEnvironment': These functions enable a set/get of a single environment value.
//      - added new function 'GetInventoryState': Allowes to check if the inventory bit is valid or not.
//      - added new function 'GetLastError': Enables the user to handle errors depending on the last error code/message.
//      - added new function 'TransferPlate': Enables the transfer of a plate between two stackers.
//      - added new function 'AdvancedOrbitalShakerGetParameters' and 'AdvancedOrbitalShakerGetParameters': Allows settings operations with the advanced orbital shaker.
//      - bugfix in function '_WaitForReady': Before resetting the error, the status is queried until the device is ready. Sending the reset command immediately after the error could lead to wrong error messages.
//      - bugfix in function 'SetEnvironment' and 'SetSpecificEnvironment': Environment values are now formated to a 1 decimal precision (xx.x). Values with bigger precision would lead to an error.
//      - bugfix in function 'UpdateInventory': If positions are set to FREE a new reset command rs:iv is used. This updates the inventory management with the right occupation status.
//      - bugfix in function 'AgitationStop' : Removed _WaitForReady. Otherwise the function would always trigger a timeout.
// ==========================================================================================================================================================================================================
#ifndef __ThermoScientific_Cytomat_Interface_hsl__
  #define __ThermoScientific_Cytomat_Interface_hsl__ 1

  #ifndef __TraceLevel_hsl__
    #include "ASWStandard\\TraceLevel\\TraceLevel.hsl"
  #endif

  #ifndef __ASWGLOBAL_hsl__
    #include "ASWStandard\\ASWGlobal\\ASWGlobal.hsl"
  #endif

  #ifndef __Hamilton_DriverTools_hsl__
    #include "Hamilton DriverTools\\Hamilton DriverTools.hsl"
  #endif

  #ifndef __Hamilton_SerialInterface_hsl__
    #include "Hamilton SerialInterface\\Hamilton SerialInterface.hsl"
  #endif

  namespace ThermoScientific_Cytomat_Interface
  {

    namespace CytomatType
    {
      const variable Unknown                                            (0);
      const variable C2_LINEAR                                          (1);
      const variable C5                                                 (2);
      const variable C10                                                (3);
      const variable C24                                                (4);
    }

    namespace EnvironmentType
    {
        const variable TEMPERATURE                                      (1);
        const variable HUMIDITY                                         (2);
        const variable CO2                                              (3);
        const variable O2                                               (4);
    }

    namespace ResponseType
    {
      const private variable INTEGER                                    (0);
      const private variable FLOAT                                      (1);
      const private variable STRING                                     (2);
    }

    namespace OccupationStatus
    {
      const variable FREE                                               (0);
      const variable OCCUPIED                                           (1);
    }

    namespace TransferStation
    {
      const variable POSITION_1                                         (1);
      const variable POSITION_2                                         (2);
    }

    namespace RotationDirection
    {
      const variable Clockwise                                          (1);
      const variable Counterclockwise                                   (2);
    }
    // requests
    const static variable CMD_SHAKER_STATUS                             ("ch:as");
    const static variable CMD_ERROR_STATUS                              ("ch:be");
    const static variable CMD_OVERVIEW_STATUS                           ("ch:bo");
    const static variable CMD_STATUS                                    ("ch:bs");
    const static variable CMD_GETLABWARE_ID                             ("ch:bx");
    const static variable CMD_GETINVENTORY_CHARACTERS                   ("ch:cb");
    const static variable CMD_DEVICETYPE                                ("ch:dn");
    const static variable CMD_CO2                                       ("ch:ic");
    const static variable CMD_HUMIDITY                                  ("ch:ih");
    const static variable CMD_O2                                        ("ch:io");
    const static variable CMD_INVENTORY_SCAN_STATUS                     ("ch:is");
    const static variable CMD_TEMPERATURE                               ("ch:it");
    const static variable CMD_OPTIONS_REGISTER                          ("ch:op");
    const static variable CMD_SHAKER_PARAMETER                          ("ch:pb");
    const static variable CMD_GET_FREE_STORAGE_CAPACITY                 ("ch:pf");
    const static variable CMD_STORAGE_CAPACITY                          ("ch:pm");
    const static variable CMD_OCCUPATION_STATUS                         ("ch:sd");
    const static variable CMD_GET_STACKER                               ("ch:sn");
    const static variable CMD_GET_LEVELS                                ("ch:sx");
    const static variable CMD_GET_SENSOR_STATUS                         ("ch:ts");

    // low level commands
    const static variable LL_CO2                                        ("ll:ic");
    const static variable LL_HUMIDITY                                   ("ll:ih");
    const static variable LL_INITIALIZE                                 ("ll:in");
    const static variable LL_O2                                         ("ll:io");
    const static variable LL_TEMPERATURE                                ("ll:it");
    const static variable LL_SHAKER_START                               ("ll:va");
    const static variable LL_SHAKER_STOP                                ("ll:vd");
    const static variable LL_INITIALIZE_TOS                             ("ll:vi");
    const static variable LL_MOVE_WP                                    ("ll:wp");
    const static variable LL_CLAMP_OPEN                                 ("ll:xd");
    const static variable LL_CLAMP_CLOSE                                ("ll:xa");

    // high level commands
    const static variable HL_GET_PLATE_ID                               ("mv:po");
    const static variable HL_GET_PLATE                                  ("mv:st");
    const static variable HL_INVENTORY_SCAN                             ("mv:sc");
    const static variable HL_LOCATION_SCAN                              ("mv:sn");
    const static variable HL_MOVE_PLATE_TO_WAITPOSITION                 ("mv:sw");
    const static variable HL_STORE_PLATE_FROM_WAITPOSITION              ("mv:ws");
    const static variable HL_STORE_PLATE                                ("mv:ts");

